      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a different argument expansion to C++ code. args refers to the bazel concept of [args](https://bazel.build/rules/lib/builtins/Args), which corresponds to the crate args.\n\n```\nargs \u003d ctx.actions.args()\nargs.add_all(\"--files\", ctx.files.sources)\nargs.add_all(ctx.files.public, format_each\u003d\"--header\u003d%s\")\nreturn [GnSubstitutionInfo(foo \u003d ctx.actions.args())\n```\n\nIf in your GN toolchain you have the command:\n```\ntool(\"cc\") {\n  command \u003d \"clang++ ... {starlark:foo}\"\n}\n```\n\nIt should expand to `clang++ ... --files foo.cc bar.cc --header\u003dfoo.h --header\u003dbar.h`.",
